    "abstract": "A correction refers to a change to their article that the author wishes to publish after publication. The publication of this article is subject to Frontiers' editorial approval.\u2022 Please read through all the templates before choosing \u2022 Pick the most relevant text template(s) from the following page and delete all others.\u2022 Edit the text as necessary, ensuring that the original incorrect text is included for the record, please see the below. \u2022 Please do not use any extra formatting when editing the templates, and only modify the red text unless absolutely necessary \u2022 Submit to Frontiers following the instructions on this page.When the original text contained incorrect information, to preserve the scientific record, please include that text when editing the below templates. For example:There was a mistake in the Funding statement, an incorrect number was used.The correct number is \"2015C03Bd051.\". The publisher apologizes for this mistake.The original version of this article has been updated.",
    "field": "Climate change vulnerability assessment",
    "problem": "This paper addresses the challenge of holistically assessing climate change vulnerability by integrating qualitative local perceptions with quantitative frameworks, which are often considered separately, leading to an incomplete understanding of real-world risks in rural territories.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a method combining participatory territorial diagnosis with the Livelihood Vulnerability Index (LVI-IPCC) to quantitatively assess climate change vulnerability in rural Tunisia based on local perceptions.",
    "task": "The task is to correct the funding statement for a study that assessed climate change vulnerability in rural Tunisia by combining local perceptions with quantitative analysis.",
